# Multi-species manifest. Copy to config/species.tsv to enable multi-species mode:
#   gwiscan run           # runs every species below as an independent parallel job
# Each species writes into its own results/<Prefix>/; the prefix also prefixes
# the systematic domain ids (e.g. AthGNA001.1). Proteome paths are relative to the
# project directory (or absolute). Throttle concurrency with SPECIES_PARALLEL.
#
# Annotation is optional: that species' REPRESENTATIVE GTF/GFF3 -- the same
# one-transcript-per-gene set its proteome comes from -- giving every member its
# chromosome, start, end and strand for the chromosomal distribution figure. Leave
# the cell empty for a species whose annotation you do not have; that species is
# still analysed, only without chromosomal coordinates.
Prefix	Proteome	Annotation
Ath	genomes/Athaliana.fasta	genomes/Athaliana.gtf
Gma	genomes/Gmax.fasta	genomes/Gmax.gtf
